=== Sarah died
--- The Years of the Life of Sarah
kicker: vv. 1–2
sub: Abraham Came to Mourn for Sarah
scripture: Genesis 23:1-2 | mark: an hundred and seven and twenty years old
p: Finally, Sarah having seen her son born of a miracle and come to be offered as a sacrifice, (I believe at 33 upon a hill in Jerusalem, spared by God, a picture of Jesus) she passes away a year later, at 127 years old and is honored, being given a place with the patriarchs, our being told of her end, chronicled by scripture. And in her faith, she was saved, and through her, all nations and kindreds were blessed.

--- Through Faith Also Sara Herself
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 23:1
fig: Hebrews 11:11-12 | Hebrews 11:11-12
fig: Hebrews 11:13 | Hebrews 11:13
callout: [[Hebrews 11:11-16|Read Hebrews 11:11–16]]

--- Mother Sarah
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 23:1, continued
p: Mother Sarah, as much as Mary, is blessed by God, given the honor of the seed, which is Jesus Christ. Announced by God, Himself. Brought to conceive by a miracle.
fig: Genesis 21:1-2 | Genesis 21:1-2
fig: Luke 1:30-31 | Luke 1:30-31
callout: [[Luke 1:28-37|Read Luke 1:28–37]]

--- Bookends of Faith
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 23:1, continued
fig: Luke 1:72-73 | Luke 1:72-73
callout: Like Sarah was visited by the Lord God and bore Isaac, so too was Israel visited by God in Christ Jesus, through Mary. Bookends of faith, a covenant fulfilled. [[Luke 1:68-79|Read Luke 1:68–79]]

